  "faqTitle": "FAQ",
  "faqSubtitle": "Short answers, no marketing.",
  "faqQ1": "Does it actually work?",
  "faqA1": "On the Neo 2 it boots, VRShell runs, head tracking is live and the VR display shows a real picture. The status page keeps the current list.",
  "faqQ2": "Is it safe to flash?",
  "faqA2": "There is real risk. Only the system partition gets flashed - writing a bootloader image older than the anti-rollback fuse allows hard-bricks sdm845 permanently. Read the docs flashing guide first.",
  "faqQ3": "Which headset does it run on?",
  "faqA3": "The Pico Neo 2 (A7B10 / PICOA7B10) - the first supported device, and the only one for now. Both the Eye and non-Eye SKUs work; eye tracking is extra work on top. The OS itself is built to run across vendors, with more headsets planned as the driver layer splits out.",
  "faqQ4": "Where do Pico's proprietary files come from?",
  "faqA4": "From your own device or its stock OTA. The overlay repo carries a manifest of every blob needed - path, size, sha256 prefix, purpose - and none of them are committed to source repos.",
  "faqQ5": "What is vrhome?",
  "faqA5": "Our own VR home environment. Stock VRShell needs the closed Pico compositor; vrhome is a NativeActivity that puts 2D apps on floating panels and still launches real VR apps fullscreen.",
  "faqQ6": "What is the license?",
  "faqA6": "Everything we wrote is AGPL-3.0. Dumped Pico and vendor binaries remain property of their owners and live in dump repos for research only.",

  "aboutTitle": "About",
  "aboutSubtitle": "One OS, many headsets, every step in the open.",
  "aboutWhatTitle": "What it is",
  "aboutWhatBody": "Hibiscus is a custom operating system for standalone VR headsets, built on LineageOS 17.1 - Android 10 via a phh GSI. The Pico Neo 2, a headset that shipped with Android 8.1 and a heavily proprietary VR stack, is the first supported device and where all development happens today.",
  "aboutHowTitle": "How it works",
  "aboutHowBody": "GSI plus overlay plus your own Pico stack. The vendor partition is never touched, so every compatibility problem - the vold deadlock, the missing sound card, the ABI breaks - gets fixed on the system side with init rules and shim libraries.",
  "aboutGroupTitle": "The monorepo",
  "aboutGroupBody": "Everything lives in one repo on GitLab, one directory per component: the device tree, the shims, the research notes, the dumps, the VR home and this site.",
  "aboutLicenseTitle": "License",
  "aboutLicenseBody": "All original work is AGPL-3.0. Proprietary Pico and vendor binaries in dump repos belong to their owners and are never redistributed. The Inter typeface bundled on this site is under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.",
  "aboutRepoCta": "GitLab repo",
