  "cteTitle": "HCTE",
  "cteSubtitle": "Hibiscus Controller Testing Environment - the desktop companion for Hibiscus headsets.",
  "cteWhatTitle": "What it is",
  "cteWhatBody": "HCTE is a desktop app (Linux, Windows, macOS) that pairs with a headset running Hibiscus and puts the whole development surface in one window. Plug in over USB or connect over Wi-Fi - no extra setup on the PC beyond adb, or none at all when the on-device CTE service is enabled.",
  "cteFeatOverviewTitle": "Device and controller overview",
  "cteFeatOverviewBody": "What the headset is - model, driver target, Android and Hibiscus versions, tracking mode - plus which controllers are paired, their battery and tracking state.",
  "cteFeatDisplayTitle": "Screen mirror",
  "cteFeatDisplayBody": "A live view of the headset's display at a few frames per second, enough to watch boot behavior and debug panels without wearing the headset.",
  "cteFeatInstallTitle": "APK install",
  "cteFeatInstallBody": "Push an APK to the device with one click, over adb or the socket channel.",
  "cteFeatTrackingTitle": "Live 6DoF/3DoF tracking",
  "cteFeatTrackingBody": "The head pose stream straight off the runtime: orientation, position, sample rate, a top-down trail, and per-controller poses.",
  "cteFeatDebugTitle": "Debug surface",
  "cteFeatDebugBody": "The full getprop table and a rolling logcat tail, for when something needs poking.",
  "cteConnectTitle": "How it connects",
  "cteConnectBody": "Two transports: adb over USB or wireless adb for the full feature set, and the on-device cted service on port 7340 when you don't want adb involved at all. cted is off by default and starts when you ask for it - setprop persist.hibiscus.cted 1 - same opt-in stance as wireless adb.",
  "cteGetTitle": "Getting it",
  "cteGetBody": "Desktop bundles ship with every cte-v* release on the monorepo - tarballs and zips for Linux, Windows, and macOS, mirrored to the GitLab release page so they never expire.",
  "cteReleasesCta": "CTE releases",
  "cteSourceCta": "Source"
